* TPB       108 12201  FAP FOR FORTRANS READ TAPE,WRITE TAPE            TPB 0001
*      FAP                                                              NUTPB002
*NUTPB N.Y.U. SUBROUTINE.  A FAP PROGRAM WHICH WHEN USED BU A FAP PROG. NUTPB003
*              THROUGH THE USE OF THE CALL PSEUDO-OP MAKES FROTRAN I/O  NUTPB004
*              SUBROUTINES AVAILABLE TO READ AND WRITE BINARY TAPES.    NUTPB005
*              THE TWO ENTRIES ARE                                      NUTPB006
*      1. CALL NURABT,T,R1,S1,R2,S2,.....,RN,SN    (READ A BINARY TAPE) NUTPB007
*      2. CALL NUWABT,T,W1,S1,W2,S2,.....,WN,SN    (WRITE A BINARY TAPE)NUTPB008
*      WHERE     T  IS THE TAPE NUMBER SUCH AS 2,6,8,ETC.               NUTPB009
*                W  ARE THE ITEMS TO BE WRITTEN                         NUTPB010
*                R   ARE THE ITEMS TO BE READ                           NUTPB011
*              S  ARE THE SUCCESSIVE NUMBERS OF W (OR R) ITEMS AFFECTED NUTPB012
*      SPECIAL NOTE... THIS ROUTINE (WITH THE SAME ENTRY POINT NAMES) ISNUTPB013
*              ALREADY A PART OF NUSNUP, A LARGER SUB-ROUINE WHICH      NUTPB014
*              PROVIDES ENTRIES TO PERFORM ALL FORTRAN I/O OPERATIONS.  NUTPB015
       COUNT   95                                                       NUTPB016
       ENTRY   NURABT                                 (READ A BIN. TAPE)NUTPB017
       ENTRY   NUWABT                             (WRITE A BIN. TAPE)   NUTPB018
*      ***    IF STANDARD ERROR PROCEDURE NOT IN SYSTEM MAKE THIS A PZE NUTPB019
*      ***   AND MAKE THIS  A    BCI  1,NUTPB                           NUTPB020
NURABT CAL     ATSLI              A TSX (SLI),4                         NUTPB021
       SLW     TOSLR                                                    NUTPB022
       CAL     ATRLR         TSX RLR,4                                  NUTPB023
       SLW     RESTOR+1                                                 NUTPB024
       CAL     ATTSB         TSX TSB,4                                  NUTPB025
       SLW     TOCALL                                                   NUTPB026
       TRA     SAVER                                                    NUTPB027
NUWABT CAL     ATSLO              A TSX (SLO),4                         NUTPB028
       SLW     TOSLR                                                    NUTPB029
       CAL     ATWLR         TSX WLR,4                                  NUTPB030
       SLW     RESTOR+1                                                 NUTPB031
       CAL     ATSTB         TSX STB,4                                  NUTPB032
       SLW     TOCALL                                                   NUTPB033
 SAVER SXA     SAV2,2                                                   NUTPB034
       SXA     SAV1,1                                                   NUTPB035
       AXT     SAVER,1                                                  NUTPB036
       SXD     NURABT-2,4                                               NUTPB037
       LXD     NURABT-2,2                                               NUTPB038
       CLA     ANOP         FOR INITIAL ENTRY CONDITIONS                NUTPB039
       STO     TOCALL-1                                                 NUTPB040
       CLA     1,2           TAPE NUMBER                                NUTPB041
       ALS     18                                                       NUTPB042
       STO     TAPNU                                                    NUTPB043
 TNARG CAL     2,2                                                      NUTPB044
       ARS     15                                                       NUTPB045
       LAS     ATSXZ         IS NEXT ARG A TSX WITH A TAG OF ZERO       NUTPB046
 TREST TRA     RESTOR                                                   NUTPB047
       TRA     *+2           YES                                        NUTPB048
       TRA     RESTOR        NO                                         NUTPB049
       CLA     2,2           ADD ONE TO LOC. OF ARRAY FOR FORTRAN RTNS  NUTPB050
       ADD     AONE                                                     NUTPB051
       STA     LCARY                                                    NUTPB052
 AGAIN CAL     3,2           NUMBER OF ITEMS IN ARRAY                   NUTPB053
       ARS     15                                                       NUTPB054
       LAS     ATSXZ                                                    NUTPB055
       TRA     RESTOW        IF NOT GIVEN AS LAST ARG. SUPPLY A ONE     NUTPB056
       TRA     *+2                                                      NUTPB057
       TRA     RESTOW        SEE ABOVE                                  NUTPB058
       CLA     3,2           NUMBER OF ITEMS IN ARRAY                   NUTPB059
 STRSZ STA     LCSZE                                                    NUTPB060
       CAL     TAPNU         A WORD THAT HAS THE TAPE NUMBER IN THE DECRNUTPB061
       NOP      INITIALLY=NOP, THEREAFTER A TRA TOSLR                   NUTPB062
TOCALL TSX     **,4     TO $(TSB) OR $(STB)                             NUTPB063
TOSLR  TSX     **,4          TO $(SLI) OR $(SLO)                        NUTPB064
 LCARY PZE     **            LOC. + 1 OF ARRAY                          NUTPB065
 LCSZE PZE     **            NUMBER OF ITEMS IN ARRAY                   NUTPB066
       CLA     TTOSLR           A TRA TOSLR                             NUTPB067
       STO     TOCALL-1      IF MORE ARGUMENTS SKIP THE TSX TO CALL.PROGNUTPB068
       TXI     TNARG,2,-2    PICK UP NEXT ARGYMENTS                     NUTPB069
*                                                                       NUTPB070
RESTOW TXI     *+1,2,1       IF LAST ARG. NOT GIVEN ADJUST X2 FOR       NUTPB071
       CLA     AONE          COORECT RETURN AND SUPPLY A ONE FOR SIZE   NUTPB072
       TRA     STRSZ                                                    NUTPB073
       REM                                                              NUTPB074
RESTOR TXL     NOLIST,1,SAVER                                           NUTPB075
       TSX     **,4                                                     NUTPB076
       STZ     LCARY                                                    NUTPB077
       PXA     0,2                                                      NUTPB078
 SAV2  AXT     **,2                                                     NUTPB079
 SAV1  AXT     **,1                                                     NUTPB080
       PAX     0,4                                                      NUTPB081
       TRA     2,4                                                      NUTPB082
       REM                                                              NUTPB083
 AONE  PZE     1,0,0                                                    NUTPB084
 ATSXZ OCT     0074000                                                  NUTPB085
 ATSLI TSX     $(SLI),4                                                 NUTPB086
 ATSLO TSX     $(SLO),4                                                 NUTPB087
 ATRLR TSX     $(RLR),4                                                 NUTPB088
 ATWLR TSX     $(WLR),4                                                 NUTPB089
 ATTSB TSX     $(TSB),4                                                 NUTPB090
 ATSTB TSX     $(STB),4                                                 NUTPB091
ATREST TRA     RESTOR+2                                                 NUTPB092
 TAPNU PZE                                                              NUTPB093
TTOSLR TRA     TOSLR                                                    NUTPB094
 ANOP  NOP                                                              NUTPB095
NOLIST TXI     *+1,1,1                                                  NUTPB096
       CAL     RESTOR+1                                                 NUTPB097
       SLW     TOSLR                                                    NUTPB098
       CAL     ATREST                                                   NUTPB099
       SLW     LCARY                                                    NUTPB100
       TRA     STRSZ+1                                                  NUTPB101
       END                                                              NUTPB102
 THE FOLLOWING TWO CARDS SHOULD BE SUBSTITUTED IN THE DECK IF ASSEMBLY *NUTPB103
  IS MADE WITH A SYSTEM WHICH DOES NOT CONTAIN THE STANDARD ERROR PRO- *NUTPB104
 CEDURE.  THE PROGRAM STORES INDEX 4 IN THE PLACE OCCUPIED BY THE PZE. *NUTPB105
       PZE       TO BE USED IF STANDARD ERROR NOT IN SYSTEM.  NUTPB019  NUTPB106
       BCI     1,NUTPB   USE IF STANDARD ERROR NOT IN SYSTEM   NUTPB020 NUTPB107
**************    LAST CARD NUTPB                                      *NUTPB108
